# Manifest Log — append-only completion tracking
# Format: TIMESTAMP | AGENT | STATUS | DETAILS
# 
# This file is the SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for project state.
# Every entry is immediately committed to git after writing.
#
# Status values:
#   INITIALIZED  — project created
#   INTAKE_COMPLETE — Phase 0 done, moving to research
#   RESEARCH_COMPLETE — Phase 1 done, all researchers returned
#   PLAN_APPROVED — Phase 2 done, user confirmed plan
#   TASK_REGISTERED — a task was created in Phase 2 (one entry per task)
#   STARTED — worker began a task
#   DONE — task fully complete (worker shipped, or gate passed)
#   BLOCKED — worker cannot proceed (dependency or build loop)
#   REJECTED — SecArch rejected the task
#   CONDITION_OPEN — SecArch returned APPROVED_WITH_CONDITIONS (one entry per condition)
#   CONDITION_CLOSED — that condition has been remediated (one entry per condition)
#   FAIL — Tester found failures
#   ESCALATED — exceeded retry budget, user notified
#   SHIPPED — Phase 6 complete, project delivered
#   STUCK — worker inactive >120s with no git activity (stuck retry loop or crash)
#   TEAM_SHIPPED — all charter tasks complete, team workflow finished
#
# ── STATUS DISCIPLINE (do not violate) ────────────────────────────────────────
# STATUS must be EXACTLY one of the values above. Never write free text, and never
# write a future-tense action, as a STATUS or as a standalone entry.
#
# This log records ONLY state transitions that have ALREADY HAPPENED. It is not a
# plan and not a scratchpad. Planning notes, intended next steps, and in-progress
# reasoning go in `.agent-project/notes.md`.
#
# Why this rule exists: a run once ended with the final manifest line reading
# "applying conditions as cleanup commit, then push, then copy to toolkit". That was
# an intention, never executed — but it is structurally indistinguishable from a
# completion record, so the abandoned run looked mid-flight for six days and four
# security conditions went unremediated. A future-tense note in this file is a defect.
#
# ── MACHINE-CHECKABLE INVARIANTS ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are greppable from git history with no in-context knowledge. Check them
# before SHIPPED or TEAM_SHIPPED:
#
#   1. Every registered task is done:
#      [ "$(grep -c '| TASK_REGISTERED |' manifest.log)" -eq "$(grep -c '| DONE |' manifest.log)" ]
#
#   2. Every raised condition is closed:
#      [ "$(grep -c '| CONDITION_OPEN |' manifest.log)" -eq "$(grep -c '| CONDITION_CLOSED |' manifest.log)" ]
#
#   3. A run with DONE entries and no SHIPPED entry is ABANDONED, not in progress.
#      Startup checks this before creating a new project (see SKILL.md Startup).
#
# Entry shapes for the paired statuses:
#   <timestamp> | architect        | TASK_REGISTERED  | <task_id>
#   <timestamp> | secarch-<task>   | CONDITION_OPEN   | <condition_id> | <description>
#   <timestamp> | worker-<task>    | CONDITION_CLOSED | <condition_id>
#
# Recovery: If a session dies, read this log + git log to reconstruct state.
# Rule: Never merge a branch whose worker has no DONE entry here.
# Rule: Every write to this file is followed by: git add + git commit
#
